! `alas-piezo-tiny-paw.in` with the crystal's point group kept, so that the same
! unshifted `2 2 2` sample reduces from eight k-points to **three**.
!
! The pair is the PAW counterpart of `alas-piezo-tiny.in` and its wedge, and it
! exists because the wedge completion has a PAW half that nothing exercised.
! On an augmented dataset the density moves with the strain at frozen states, so
! the mixed second derivative carries a term quadratic in a per-k tangent, and a
! wedge sum of a product is not the product of the full-zone objects: one factor
! has to be made whole before it is contracted, which is
! `_full_zone_field_response` on the grid and `_full_zone_becsum_response` in the
! one-centre terms. Averaging the finished rank-3 tensor cannot repair it, which
! is why agreeing with the closed grid is the check and why the test runs the
! same wedge with the completion switched off as its falsifier.
!
! Three k-points is not a converged sample and is not meant to be: what is read
! here is an identity between two k-sets of the same unshifted grid, which holds
! at any cutoff and on any mesh, so the cell is chosen for cost.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.6134, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 10.0, ecutrho = 44.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al 26.98 Al.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.1.0.0.UPF
 As 74.92 As.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Al 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 2 2 2 0 0 0
